@startuml
title Heima v3 - Support, Learning, and Delivery Governance
left to right direction

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam ArrowColor #3C4043
skinparam componentBorderColor #3C4043
skinparam packageBorderColor #80868B

package "Foundation slice" {
  component "Layer 0\nPersistence, continuity, follow-up outbox,\nTiming, runtime health" as L0 #E6F4EA
  component "Layer 1\nHouseFact, Provenance,\nLocation, Zone, Topology" as L1 #E6F4EA
}

component "Layer 2\nstaged registry generation\nSensors, FusionRules, Actuators" as L2 #E6F4EA
component "Layer 3\nhistorical learning, artifacts,\nfindings, signals, candidates" as L3 #E6F4EA
component "Layer 4\nSemantic DAG\nauthorized signal consumer" as L4 #E6F4EA
component "Layer 5\ncandidate review, configured Reaction,\naction admissibility" as L5 #E6F4EA
component "Layer 6\nnotification kinds and adapters, AvailabilityEpisodeTracker,\nquiet hours, digests, delivery" as L6 #E6F4EA
component "Layer 8\nrole-based panel, change sets,\nhistory, explanations, published entities" as L8 #E6F4EA

L0 --> L3 : bounded fact-history reads\nand runtime-health snapshot
L2 -[#1A73E8,dashed]-> L3 : staged registry generation
L1 -[#1A73E8,dashed]-> L3 : immutable fact and location contracts

L3 --> L4 : one authorized, expiring\nInferenceSignal
L3 --> L5 : LearningProposalCandidate\nfor independent validation and review

L3 --> L6 : typed suppression occurrence
L4 --> L6 : typed suppression occurrence
L5 --> L6 : typed suppression occurrence
L5 --> L6 : typed follow-up intent and occurrence
L3 -[#1A73E8,dashed]-> L6 : staged owner declaration
L4 -[#1A73E8,dashed]-> L6 : staged owner declaration only
L5 -[#1A73E8,dashed]-> L6 : staged automation binding
L5 --> L6 : advisory, action-notice,\nproposal-review and consent occurrences
L0 --> L6 : recovery-confirmation occurrence
L6 --> L0 : sole producer of the seven\nnotification event facts, with outbox records
L6 --> L0 : answers to the response ingress
L8 --> L0 : change sets through the\ncomposed generation
L8 --> L5 : governance commands
L8 --> L3 : signal adoption commands

note bottom of L3
  Historical learning and model work use the slow path.
  Authorized bounded signals may serve the current DAG;
  no HA runtime reads, blocking I/O, or direct action.
end note

note bottom of L5
  Candidate kind/version and Reaction-descriptor payload
  are validated independently. Learning proposes;
  policy review and action authority stay here.
end note

note bottom of L6
  The tracker is transient. It reconciles active
  suppression episodes at a publication-generation swap.
  Only Layer 6 renders, delivers, and audits notifications;
  its output lengths are bounded.
end note

legend bottom
  |= Color |= Meaning |
  |<#E6F4EA> | Defined layer |
  |<#FCE8E6> | Future layer with fixed interface |
  | Solid arrow | Typed data or operational hand-off |
  | <color:#1A73E8>Blue dashed arrow</color> | Immutable contract or staging dependency |
endlegend
@enduml
